Two names cxx1 emits and cl does not, and no name that differs: the vftables `??_7PV@@6B@` and `??_7PW@@6B@`. The Microsoft ABI has no key function - a vftable is emitted, COMDAT, by every translation unit that constructs the class - and nothing here constructs a PV or a PW, so cl emits neither; cxx1 emits a polymorphic class's vftable where the class is defined. Every name for the classes this case is about - the 45 with empty bases and no virtuals - agrees with cl.
